#====================================================================
# E252 — Asset-gated libraries need substantive pre-asset consumer tests
#====================================================================

id:                     E252
trigger_tool:           conan_test|ctest|cmake|cc|clang
phase:                  compilation|linking|testing
error_signature:        version-only smoke passes while context API is unusable|test requires redistributing unavailable runtime assets|missing-asset path is unverified

severity:               2
category:               testing|public-api|external-assets|consumer-contract
match_keywords:         version-only smoke, ROM, firmware, model data, external asset, context lifecycle, missing asset, public inventory, consumer test
title:                  Asset-gated libraries need substantive pre-asset consumer tests

root_cause:             Libraries that require user-supplied ROMs, firmware, models, or licensed data for their full workload still expose meaningful installed-package contracts before those assets are loaded. Testing only a version function proves linkage but misses allocation, inventory, configuration, cleanup, and explicit missing-asset behavior. Bundling invented or redistributable-looking substitutes would test a different contract and can violate provenance or licensing boundaries.
affected_scope:         C/C++ libraries whose complete runtime workflow depends on external user-provided assets that cannot lawfully or faithfully be included in a package test.
verification_cmd:       conan create <recipe> -pr:h=<target-profile> -pr:b=<target-profile> --build=<package>

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           substantive-pre-asset-lifecycle-flow
rec_description:        Keep the lawful asset boundary explicit. In one installed-package consumer, call real public inventory and capability queries, create and release the primary context, exercise reversible configuration, and require the documented missing-asset result without changing the context to an open or active state. Run the process under the generated package environment. Count the process as one logical flow; its internal semantic checks are assertions, not extra tests.
rec_command:            <consumer> && verify exactly one successful process exit
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               installed-pre-asset-context-consumer

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      compile-link-plus-explicit-gap
fallback_description:   If even context creation needs restricted assets, compile and link a real public consumer, record target execution as unresolved, and do not claim functional runtime coverage until lawful assets are supplied.
fallback_command:
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:

forbid_1_pattern:       (version|get_version).*(only|smoke)|return\s+0.*(ROM|firmware|model|asset)
forbid_1_reason:        A version-only or constant-success process does not exercise the installed library's stateful public contract.
forbid_1_consequence:   Packaging and ABI failures remain hidden until a downstream application supplies real assets.
forbid_2_pattern:       (assertion_count|check_count).*test_(count|flow)|shared.*\+.*static.*logical
forbid_2_reason:        Internal checks and shared/static reruns do not create independent inputs or failure boundaries.
forbid_2_consequence:   Reported coverage is inflated without additional executable workflows.

principles:             P005

causes:                 []
caused_by:              []
similar_to:             []
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        []

